.TITLE "grep"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Searches for specific __patterns__ within files using regular expressions. It is an essential tool for __filtering__ data and finding information in large text files.

.DIV "TLDR"
**grep "pattern" file**
Searches for a specific string or pattern inside a file.
> __"pattern"__ the search term | __file__ the target file

**grep -i "pattern" file**
Performs a search while ignoring whether characters are uppercase or lowercase.
> __-i__ ignore case flag | __"pattern"__ the search term

**grep -v "pattern" file**
Displays only the lines that do not match the specified pattern.
> __-v__ invert match flag | __"pattern"__ the search term

**grep -r "pattern" folder**
Searches for a pattern recursively within all files in a directory.
> __-r__ recursive flag | __"pattern"__ search term | __folder__ directory path

**grep -n "pattern" file**
Displays the line numbers along with the matching text.
> __-n__ line number flag | __"pattern"__ search term

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __grep__ in combination with other commands via pipes (|) allows for powerful data processing. For more complex searches, consider using the __-E__ flag to enable extended regular expressions.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
